,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-05-26T03:09:26.655052"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-05-26T03:09:26.655052"}}},"ISBN:9780195679014":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780195679014","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7394883M/Martyrdom_in_the_Sikh_Tradition","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7394883M/Martyrdom_in_the_Sikh_Tradition","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1130186-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Oxford University Press, USA"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subtitle":"Playing the 'Game of Love' (Oxford India Paperbacks)","source_records":["amazon:0195679016:14:597945196:157723","bwb:9780195679014"],"title":"Martyrdom in the Sikh Tradition","number_of_pages":326,"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-20T01:59:28.882195"},"covers":[1130186],"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T13:35:46.876380"},"isbn_13":["9780195679014"],"isbn_10":["0195679016"],"publish_date":"October 28, 2005","key":"/books/OL7394883M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2486728A","name":"Louis E. Fenech"}],"latest_revision":4,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL224181W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"revision":4}},"ISBN:9780195649475":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780195649475","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL6874636M/Martyrdom_in_the_Sikh_tradition","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL6874636M/Martyrdom_in_the_Sikh_tradition","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/4603586-S.jpg","details":{"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"identifiers":{"librarything":["5137630"]},"title":"Martyrdom in the Sikh tradition","subtitle":"playing the \"game of love\"","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL2486728A","name":"Louis E. Fenech"}],"publish_date":"2000","publishers":["Oxford University Press"],"isbn_10":["0195649478"],"covers":[4603586,4542511],"lc_classifications":["BL2018.5.M37 F46 2000","BL2018.5.M37F46 2000","BL2018.5.M+"],"publish_places":["New Delhi"],"pagination":"xix, 306 p. ;","source_records":["marc:marc_records_scriblio_net/part01.dat:91820923:797","bwb:9780195649475","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part01.utf8:165915499:903","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2023-11-10:p8-crh-275","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-007.mrc:310142384:1216","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_039.bib.mrc:216190116:2479"],"lccn":["00411995"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["Martyrdom -- Sikhism","Sikhism -- Doctrines"],"publish_country":"ii ","by_statement":"Louis E. Fenech.","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P8-CRH-275"],"oclc_numbers":["46945632"],"key":"/books/OL6874636M","number_of_pages":306,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL224181W"}],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"The notion of martyrdom and the role of martyrs in religious and political history constitutes a major component in discourse among Sikhs throughout the world. Martyrdom in the Sikh Tradition examines how and why Sikhs began to represent their history as a history of persecutions and martyrdoms and began to see themselves as a 'community through whose veins flows the blood of martyrdom'. Fenech seeks the reasons why the themes of sacrifice and martyrdom came to dominate Sikh imaginations in the early twentieth century and how these understandings continue to play such a vital role in the Sikh community today. He does this through an analysis of the Sikh scriptures, eighteenth and nineteenth century Sikh literature, as well as the voluminous tracts and newspapers produced under the auspices of the late nineteenth-century 'reform' movement, the Singh Sabha.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":11,"revision":11,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-05-22T05:22:42.688276"}}},"ISBN:9780718894061":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780718894061","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL32832685M/Ecclesial_Identities_in_a_Multi-Faith_Context","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL32832685M/Ecclesial_Identities_in_a_Multi-Faith_Context","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11464590-S.jpg","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"title":"Ecclesial Identities in a Multi-Faith Context","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8538510A","name":"Darren Todd Duerksen"}],"publish_date":"Jul 30, 2015","source_records":["amazon:0718894065","bwb:9780718894061"],"number_of_pages":314,"publishers":["Lutterworth Press"],"isbn_10":["0718894065"],"isbn_13":["9780718894061"],"physical_format":"paperback","full_title":"Ecclesial Identities in a Multi-Faith Context Jesus Truth-Gatherings  among Hindus and Sikhs in Northwest India","subtitle":"Jesus Truth-Gatherings  among Hindus and Sikhs in Northwest India","notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Source title: Ecclesial Identities in a Multi-Faith Context: Jesus Truth-Gatherings (Yeshu Satsangs) among Hindus and Sikhs in Northwest India"},"covers":[11464590],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL22323858W"}],"key":"/books/OL32832685M","lc_classifications":["BR128.H5"],"latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-07-20T15:28:00.745827"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-10-05T14:03:27.283575"}}},"ISBN:9781625646552":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781625646552","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL30403762M/Ecclesial_identities_in_a_multi-faith_context","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL30403762M/Ecclesial_identities_in_a_multi-faith_context","details":{"publishers":["Pickwick Publications"],"table_of_contents":[{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Precedent literature: early pioneers and present scholars of contemporary Yeshu satsangs","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Social theory framework: an emergentist theory of identity formation","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Ethnographic methodology","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"An introduction to Yeshu satsangs and their context","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Structural emergent properties of Hindu/Sikh practices","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Inscribing new cultural emergent properties on Hindu and Sikh practices","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Resisting and reshaping Christian practices","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Ecclesial identity markers of the Yeshu satsangs","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"The emergence of the Yeshu satsang's ecclesial identities","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Ecclesial identity emergence in the book of Acts","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Conclusion and recommendations","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Appendix A. Delimiting region versus religion","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Appendix B. Summary of Yeshu satsangis and leaders","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Appendix C. Leadership questionnaire","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Appendix D. Satsangi questionnaire","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Appendix E. Summary of Yeshu satsang leaders by community","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}},{"level":0,"label":"","title":"Appendix F. The use of bhajans by Yeshu satsangs.","pagenum":"","type":{"key":"/type/toc_item"}}],"isbn_10":["1625646550"],"series":["American Society of Missiology monograph series -- vol. 22","American Society of Missiology monograph series -- 22."],"lc_classifications":["BR1155 .D89 2015","BR1155.D89 2015"],"key":"/books/OL30403762M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8538510A","name":"Darren Todd Duerksen"}],"subtitle":"Jesus truth-gatherings (Yeshu satsangs) among Hindus and Sikhs in northwest India","publish_places":["Eugene, Oregon"],"contributions":["Dyrness, William A., writer of foreword"],"isbn_13":["9781625646552"],"pagination":"xxiii, 292 pages","source_records":["marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part42.utf8:108234130:2749","bwb:9781625646552","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-023.mrc:157512479:2704","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_034.bib.mrc:89401535:6853"],"title":"Ecclesial identities in a multi-faith context","lccn":["2015301410"],"notes":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Revision of author's thesis (Ph. D.)--Fuller Theological Seminary, 2011.\n\nIncludes bibliographical references (pages 279-287) and index."},"number_of_pages":292,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subject_places":["Northwestern India"],"subjects":["Hindus","Identification (Religion)","Christianity and culture","Relations","Christianity","Religion","Christians","Hinduism","Sikhs","Christianity and other religions","Sikhism"],"publish_date":"2015","publish_country":"oru","copyright_date":"2015","by_statement":"Darren Todd Duerksen ; foreword by William A. Dyrness","oclc_numbers":["900306795"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL22323858W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"When Hindus and Sikhs become followers of Christ, what happens next? Should they join Christian churches that often look and feel very unfamiliar to them? Or to what degree can or should they remain a part of their Hindu/Sikh communities and practices? Uncomfortable with the answers that were provided to them by Christian leaders in northwest India, six followers of Christ began Yeshu satsangs (Jesus truth-gatherings) that sought to follow Christ and the teachings of the Bible while remaining connected to their Hindu and/or Sikh communities. Ecclesial Identities in a Multi-faith Context analyzes the contextualized practices and identities of these leaders and their gatherings, situating these in the religious history of the region and the personal histories of the leaders themselves. Whereas Christians worry that the Yeshu satsangs and related \"insider movements\" are syncretizing their beliefs and are not properly identifiable as \"churches,\" Ecclesial Identities analyzes the Yeshu satsang's narratives and practices to find vibrant expressions of local church that are grappling with questions and tensions of social and religious identity. In addition to its ethnographic approach, Ecclesial Identities also utilizes recent sociological and anthropological theory in identity formation and critical realism, as well as discussion of biblical ecclesiology from the book of Acts. This study will be helpful resource for those interested in global Christianity, the practices and identities of churches in religiously plural environments, and the creative ways in which Christ-followers can missionally engage people of other faiths. - from book blurb."},"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-09-21T11:58:16.590905"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-03-29T13:14:56.490027"}}},"ISBN:9780718844165":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780718844165","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34517187M/Ecclesial_Identities_in_a_Multi-Faith_Context","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34517187M/Ecclesial_Identities_in_a_Multi-Faith_Context","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL8538510A","name":"Darren Todd Duerksen"}],"isbn_13":["9780718844165"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"number_of_pages":314,"publish_date":"2015","publishers":["Lutterworth Press, The"],"source_records":["bwb:9780718844165"],"subjects":["Chris